1
00:00:01,420 --> 00:00:05,780
Hi, I’m Athos, from Figueira.

2
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:12,800
PatientKeeper Retorno grew from problems I
see while working with medical practices:

3
00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:19,925
scattered conversations, unanswered messages,
and follow-ups that never reach

4
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:21,065
a clear conclusion.

5
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:26,080
A canceled appointment should not become a
forgotten patient.

6
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:31,220
Our goal is to help the doctor understand
what remains open,

7
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:37,340
who is responsible, and which record supports
the next step.

8
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:41,680
Everything in this demonstration uses
fictional data.

9
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:47,200
The system organizes the work, while the
doctor remains responsible for decisions.

10
00:00:47,766 --> 00:00:53,526
The doctor workspace brings the patient
journey, consultation material,

11
00:00:53,706 --> 00:00:55,366
and contact history together.

12
00:00:55,686 --> 00:01:00,946
Our fictional example follows a bunion and
bunionette surgery episode.

13
00:01:01,486 --> 00:01:08,026
The doctor records the phase, responsibility,
next administrative action,

14
00:01:08,206 --> 00:01:10,626
and a date to check progress.

15
00:01:11,047 --> 00:01:17,752
The system does not invent surgical
instructions or decide clinical timing.

16
00:01:17,767 --> 00:01:24,192
Search, a fictional calendar, three interface
languages, and light or dark appearance

17
00:01:24,206 --> 00:01:27,166
help make navigation straightforward.

18
00:01:27,886 --> 00:01:33,972
The workflow centers on the doctor, while
giving reception staff a clearer

19
00:01:33,986 --> 00:01:37,486
handoff and fewer scattered instructions.

20
00:01:39,733 --> 00:01:45,438
In the configured local version, a short
fictional audio file can be

21
00:01:45,453 --> 00:01:47,113
transcribed on the computer.

22
00:01:47,373 --> 00:01:52,578
The doctor reviews the transcript and selects
literal passages to prepare

23
00:01:52,593 --> 00:01:54,013
a source-linked draft.

24
00:01:54,433 --> 00:01:56,973
This is an extract for review,

25
00:01:57,253 --> 00:02:03,198
not an automatically generated diagnosis or a
signed medical record.

26
00:02:03,213 --> 00:02:09,218
The contact workflow checks the recorded
preference and requires review of the

27
00:02:09,233 --> 00:02:11,253
exact source and message.

28
00:02:11,693 --> 00:02:14,233
WhatsApp contact is simulated.

29
00:02:14,673 --> 00:02:16,373
No message is sent.

30
00:02:16,913 --> 00:02:23,553
A refusal blocks contact, and changing the
source invalidates the previous review.

31
00:02:24,173 --> 00:02:29,353
Preparing a message does not mean the
follow-up is complete.

32
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:38,365
We tested Gemma through AMD Token Factory and
connected PatientKeeper to an

33
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:42,600
Evolus workflow using that configured Gemma
connection.

34
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:50,784
One real application-to-API execution
returned an administrative candidate in about

35
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:56,680
eight seconds, with two exact source
citations and mandatory human review.

36
00:02:57,400 --> 00:03:00,120
The administrative state remained unchanged.

37
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:06,200
The application checks the current context
and blocks outdated results.

38
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:11,580
The doctor can inspect the original sources
before deciding what to do.

39
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:15,279
This was a small synthetic pilot.

40
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:19,444
The public demonstration displays recorded
evidence,

41
00:03:19,460 --> 00:03:22,340
without live inference or audio
transcription.

42
00:03:24,286 --> 00:03:26,746
What could this mean for a doctor’s day?

43
00:03:27,166 --> 00:03:32,066
The routine reported to us involves six
records per day,

44
00:03:32,706 --> 00:03:35,546
with fifteen minutes of documentation each.

45
00:03:35,766 --> 00:03:40,106
That represents ninety minutes of daily
documentation.

46
00:03:40,626 --> 00:03:47,186
If an assisted workflow reduced each record
to ten minutes, including preparation,

47
00:03:47,486 --> 00:03:52,426
review, and corrections, the difference would
be thirty minutes a day.

48
00:03:53,026 --> 00:03:58,111
That is an illustrative scenario, not a
measured PatientKeeper result.

49
00:03:58,126 --> 00:04:02,691
Our next step is to test that assumption in a

50
00:04:02,706 --> 00:04:04,506
controlled practice pilot.

51
00:04:05,316 --> 00:04:09,051
The administrative scaffold predates the
hackathon.

52
00:04:09,066 --> 00:04:15,231
Source review, AMD experiments, and the
doctor workspace were added

53
00:04:15,246 --> 00:04:16,571
during the event.

54
00:04:16,586 --> 00:04:24,806
PatientKeeper Retorno: a source, a
responsible doctor, and a clear next step.
